Perhaps we should do:

```java
    configureFromSystemProperties.set(log);
    try {
      configureFromSystemProperties(options, VERTX_OPTIONS_PROP_PREFIX);
      if (options.getMetricsOptions() != null) {
        configureFromSystemProperties(options.getMetricsOptions(), METRICS_OPTIONS_PROP_PREFIX);
      }
      beforeStartingVertx(options);
      builder.init();
    } finally {
      configureFromSystemProperties.set(null);
    }
```

instead of

```java
    configureFromSystemProperties.set(log);
    try {
      configureFromSystemProperties(options, VERTX_OPTIONS_PROP_PREFIX);
      if (options.getMetricsOptions() != null) {
        configureFromSystemProperties(options.getMetricsOptions(), METRICS_OPTIONS_PROP_PREFIX);
      }
      builder.init();
    } finally {
      configureFromSystemProperties.set(null);
    }

    beforeStartingVertx(options);
```

@vietj so here's a test on Vert.x 3.9 that checks you can modify `VertxOptions`:

https://github.com/eclipse-vertx/vert.x/blob/5dee3511fdb41354a5381a55ad9abb5ab5d5514a/src/test/java/io/vertx/core/impl/launcher/LauncherExtensibilityTest.java#L109-L158

Unfortunately this option has been removed in 4.0 and so has the test... But the use case of customizing options programmatically remains valid.
